{"id":"housing-per-home","title":"Federal homeless-housing budgets per home","question":"Which federally funded homeless-housing projects in San Francisco cost far more per home than the rest, and why?","finding":"In the fiscal 2026 federal renewal list, 22 San Francisco projects with a stated number of homes have a middle budget of $36,028 a home a year. 3 are at one and a half times that or more, led by Housing For Survivors at $104,284 a home, of which 56% is services rather than rent. A further 7 housing projects worth $8.3 million list no number of homes at all.","how":"Each row is a project line in the U.S. housing department's grant inventory worksheet for the San Francisco homeless-funding area: the annual renewal amount divided by the homes listed. The first-year column is the same project in the earliest worksheet on file (2021 or later).","limits":"The worksheet is the amount eligible for renewal, not money spent, and it names the City as applicant, not the nonprofit that runs each building. Rent budgets follow federal rent ceilings, so they rise with the size of the homes; projects for survivors of violence, young people and veterans carry more services. Projects that lease whole buildings or fund only services list no homes and cannot be compared.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"project","t":"Project","type":"text"},{"k":"applicant","t":"Applicant","type":"text"},{"k":"homes","t":"Homes","type":"int"},{"k":"budget","t":"Annual budget 2026","type":"usd"},{"k":"perHome","t":"Per home","type":"usd"},{"k":"timesMedian","t":"Against the middle project","type":"times"},{"k":"servicesShare","t":"Share that is services","type":"pct"},{"k":"servicesPerHome","t":"Services per home","type":"usd"},{"k":"perHomeFirst","t":"Per home, first year on file","type":"usd"},{"k":"firstYear","t":"First year","type":"year"},{"k":"change","t":"Change","type":"pct"}],"rows":[{"project":"Housing For Survivors","applicant":"City and County of San Francisco","homes":25,"budget"